      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1911-10-07_WidnesExaminer_art0110" n="art0110">
        <head>ROYAL VISIT TO INDIA.</head>
        <p>THE ROYAL VISIT TO INDIA.</p>
        <p>The preparations for the King and Queen's departure to India, on Noveinber 9th, are almost complete. The P. &amp;0. liner, "Medina," lies at Southampton ready for her historic voyage. She has been transformed from a lir er into a palatial private yacht, and the Royal apartments have been fitted up in the most luxurious style. The ship has been painted white from end to end, with a broad band of royal blue around the hull and funnels. The journey will take their Majesties through the Mediterranean ; and unkss Italy and Turkey have settled their differinces by that hose, it may mean an alteration in the King's plan,.</p>
