        <p>COUNTY PALATINE OF CHESTER. NOTICE IS HEREBY GIVEN, that the next GENERAL QUARTER SESSIONS of the Peace for the COUNTY PALATINE OF CHESTER will be . holden at the COURT•HOUSE, KNUTSFORD, in and for the mid County, on MONDAY, the 16th day of OCTOBER, 1911, at Eleven o'clock in the Forenoon, when the Grand jury will de empannelled. The hearing of all Appeals arising within the Petty Sessional Divisions of Altrincham, Bucklow, Dukin- field, hi iddles i oh, Ssuclbsob, Congleton, N nabs ich, Prestbuty and Stockport, farming the Knutsford District, and the trials of all prisoners committed from such Div isions, sill take place at such sessions. The Grand and Petty Juries for the Knutsford District must be in attendance at the COURT HOUSE, KNUTSFORD, at the opening of the Court on MONDAY, the 16th day of OCTOBER NEXT, at Eleven o'clock in the Forenoon. THE COURT sill be Adjourned to the CASTLE OF CHESTER on WEDNESDAY, the 18th day of OCTOBER, 1911, at Eleven o'clock in the Forenoon, when another Grand Jury sill be empannelled. The hearing of all Appeals arising within the Petty Sessional Divisions of Brenton, Chester Castle, Dares- bury, Eddisbnry, Nants ioh, Runcorn, Winsford and M irral, forming the Chester District, and the trisla of all prisoners committed from the last-mentioned Divisions will take place at such Adjourned Sessions. The Grand and Petty Juries for the Chester District must be in attendance at the CASTLE OF CHESTER, at the opening of the Court no WEDNESDAY, the 18th day of October, 1911. at Eleven O'clock in the Forenoon. REGINALD POTTS, Clerk of the Pratte for the County Cheater, 3rd October, 1911. Palatine of Chester.</p>
